<Layout title="Kin & Campus | Someone looking after them">
<div class="w hero2"><div><div class="eyebrow">Concierge medicine for Virginia Tech students</div><h1>Someone looking after them.</h1><p class="lead">A local, board-certified pediatrician in Blacksburg — for the years they live eight minutes from campus.</p><p><a class="btn" href={href("join")}>Reserve a spot</a> &nbsp; <a class="lnk" href={href("parents")}>For parents &rarr;</a> &nbsp; <a class="lnk" href={href("students")}>For students &rarr;</a></p></div>
<img class="art" src={href("photos/drillfield-fall.jpg")} width="678" height="452" alt="Fall leaves on the Drillfield, Burruss Hall across the green">
</div>
<div class="w"><div class="trust"><div><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-chat"/></svg><b>A number they actually have</b><span>Direct physician text. The doctor in town.</span></div><div><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-clock"/></svg><b>Same day, in Blacksburg</b><span>Eight minutes from campus. A panel small enough that same-day is real.</span></div><div><svg class="ic" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-shield"/></svg><b>You stay in the letter</b><span>Hometown doctor named on day one. The standing rule you agree on.</span></div></div></div>
<section><div class="w split"><div><div class="eyebrow">For parents</div><h2>They're far from home. We are not.</h2><p>What you want is a real person looking after your kid. A local, board-certified pediatrician. Check-ins around holidays and finals. A letter to the doctor who has known them since kindergarten.</p><p><a class="lnk" href={href("parents")}>How we look after them &rarr;</a></p></div>
<svg class="art" viewBox="0 0 600 190" role="img" aria-label="You, Kin and Campus, and your student, connected"><path d="M112 80Q190 10 265 66M335 66Q410 10 488 80" fill="none" stroke="#C9A24B" stroke-width="4" stroke-dasharray="2 10" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="70" cy="82" r="42" fill="#6B2737"/><circle cx="70" cy="70" r="12" fill="#F6EFE4"/><path d="M46 104q24-26 48 0z" fill="#F6EFE4"/><circle cx="530" cy="82" r="42" fill="#C9A24B"/><circle cx="530" cy="70" r="12" fill="#2A1A1E"/><path d="M506 104q24-26 48 0z" fill="#2A1A1E"/><circle cx="300" cy="78" r="40" fill="#9CAF98"/><path d="M272 84L300 58 328 84v22H272z" fill="#FBF7F0" stroke="#6B2737" stroke-width="3"/><rect x="293" y="90" width="14" height="16" fill="#C9A24B"/><g font-family="DM Sans,sans-serif" font-size="15" font-weight="700" fill="currentColor" text-anchor="middle"><text x="70" y="150">You</text><text x="300" y="150">Kin &amp; Campus</text><text x="530" y="150">Your student</text></g></svg></div></section>
<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="w"><div class="eyebrow">What a parent wants, in town</div><h2>Four things we hold while they're here.</h2><div class="grid"><div class="card"><div class="num">1</div><h3>Chronic care</h3><p>The plan they already have, held here. We keep it going — refills, holidays, finals, a letter home when something changes.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="num">2</div><h3>Nearby</h3><p>A trained eye, in the same town. A board-certified pediatrician who lives in Blacksburg. Watches them the way you would if you lived eight minutes from campus.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="num">3</div><h3>Now, not later</h3><p>They learn care while they're young. How to call a doctor. How to keep a plan. This is the year to start — not at forty.</p></div><div class="card"><div class="num">4</div><h3>Together</h3><p>Student, physician, and you. We figure health out in the room. You and the hometown doctor stay in the letter.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section><div class="w"><div class="eyebrow">Once you join</div><h2>A parent starts. The student keeps the number.</h2><div class="grid"><div class="card"><h3>You write us</h3><p>Tell us who is coming to Blacksburg. We follow with a call. No chart on this website.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>They meet their doctor</h3><p>An unhurried first visit in town. Long enough to start together.</p></div><div class="card"><h3>The number is theirs</h3><p>Direct text after that. Same day when something comes up. Check-ins around holidays and finals.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="band"><div class="w"><div class="eyebrow">The standing rule</div><h2>You get the rule you agree on. They decide what we share.</h2><p>At 18 the chart is theirs. We write down what to share with you, and we follow it. Their hometown doctor gets the note the same afternoon. <a class="lnk2" href={href("privacy")}>How sharing works &rarr;</a></p></div></section>
<section><div class="w"><div class="eyebrow">A note of the kind we send</div><h2>The hometown doctor stays on the page.</h2><div class="card" style="max-width:640px"><p>To the pediatrician of record · hometown</p><p>Saw them today. The plan is holding. I'll write you when it shifts — and at the end of the year, so August starts from a full page.</p><p>Your pediatrician at Kin &amp; Campus · Blacksburg</p></div></div></section>
<section><div class="w" style="text-align:center"><h2>A hundred and nineteen a month while they're on campus.</h2><p class="lead" style="margin:16px auto 28px">$1,190 for the academic year, August through May. A panel small enough that same-day is real.</p><a class="btn" href={href("join")}>Reserve a spot</a></div></section>
</Layout>
